cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Health Economics Ontology (HEO)"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heo"
repository: "https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/HEO"
abstract: "The Health Economics Ontology (HEO) is a vocabulary of health economics concepts taken from HealthEconomics.wiki, each with a permanent web address, a name and a definition. It is written in the Simple Knowledge Organization System (SKOS) and the Web Ontology Language (OWL), with typed relationships between concepts such as part of, measures and used to calculate. Concepts sit under one top concept, Health Economics, and the subdomains of the wiki. HEO describes meanings, not real things, and its companion the Real Health Economics Ontology (RHEO) describes the real world. Version 2.0.0 moves the ontology and its own terms from https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontology/heo to https://healtheconomics.wiki/ontologies/heo, to match the ontology page on the site. Concept addresses and content are unchanged."
keywords:
  - "health economics"
  - "ontology"
  - "SKOS"
  - "controlled vocabulary"
  - "thesaurus"
  - "economic evaluation"
  - "health technology assessment"
  - "linked data"
